WEBVTT

00:13.360 --> 00:15.440
Nice! Okay!

00:17.820 --> 00:19.900
Thank you very much!

00:22.360 --> 00:23.620
Excellent work.

00:23.910 --> 00:26.329
Thanks very much, Mr. Manager.

00:26.330 --> 00:30.080
This shoot's schedule is a bit
tight, but let's do our best.

00:30.460 --> 00:32.540
Sure! No problem!

00:34.960 --> 00:37.590
I've always wanted to come to Okinawa!

00:39.880 --> 00:46.559
Hi, all. I'm still here and still
doing great. And when I say "here,"

00:46.560 --> 00:51.560
I mean where I've come for my photo
shoot, which is—get this—Okinawa!

00:52.190 --> 00:56.730
Me and everyone on staff are working
hard to make this a great shoot!

01:07.530 --> 01:09.950
I'll do my absolute best!

01:13.370 --> 01:14.879
Ippai hibiki MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

01:14.880 --> 01:16.379
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

01:16.380 --> 01:17.879
Ippai todoke FEELING
Let tons of feelings reach you

01:17.880 --> 01:19.379
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

01:19.380 --> 01:20.839
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

01:20.840 --> 01:22.356
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

01:22.380 --> 01:23.969
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

01:23.970 --> 01:26.220
Super Soni LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

01:38.190 --> 01:42.650
Saikin omoitsukimashita
Lately, I've come to realize

01:44.280 --> 01:48.620
Kimochi tsutaeru tte taihen
That getting feelings across is tough

01:50.370 --> 01:55.169
Umaku dekitari dekinattari
Whether it goes well or not

01:55.170 --> 01:58.919
Muzukashii kara oku no te de
Is tough, so my trump card

01:58.920 --> 02:01.510
Mouretsu taiatari desu
Is going for it at full force

02:03.260 --> 02:05.550
Dakedo hitomishiri (hitomishiri)
But I'm shy (shy)

02:06.180 --> 02:08.980
Gomakashite senobi (senobi)
I act like it's nothing and aim high (high)

02:09.350 --> 02:10.889
Ashi ga gakuburu de
With legs trembling

02:10.890 --> 02:14.140
Hirakinaotte arinomama GO!
I get serious and just go for it!

02:14.520 --> 02:17.149
Zenkai, soukai, daitenkai Recuperation,
exhilaration, a big revolution

02:17.150 --> 02:20.190
Nandemo chokushin STRAIGHT
No matter what, keep heading straight

02:20.520 --> 02:23.189
Sekai, mankai, mugendai
The world, in full bloom, infinity

02:23.190 --> 02:26.739
Kyou mo genki ni koko ni imasu (HEY!) I'm
here again today, living to the fullest (Hey!)

02:26.740 --> 02:28.256
Ippai hibike MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

02:28.280 --> 02:29.699
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

02:29.700 --> 02:31.346
Ippai todoke FEELING?
Let tons of feelings reach you

02:31.370 --> 02:32.619
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

02:32.620 --> 02:34.289
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

02:34.290 --> 02:35.619
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

02:35.620 --> 02:37.436
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

02:37.460 --> 02:39.630
SUPER SONI LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

02:42.630 --> 02:43.510
Three full days, correct? Yes.

02:43.511 --> 02:45.196
Good morning!
Three full days, correct? Yes.

02:45.220 --> 02:47.550
We'll work out the details when we meet.

02:48.010 --> 02:49.890
Yes. Thank you very much.

02:50.180 --> 02:51.219
Sonico.

02:51.220 --> 02:54.470
Oh, hi Ouka. Good morning.

02:54.980 --> 02:56.180
You here for a job?

02:56.430 --> 02:59.900
No, I'm here today to confirm my schedule.

03:00.270 --> 03:02.360
Couldn't you have done that by e-mail?

03:03.690 --> 03:10.369
Mr. Computer isn't really doing what I ask him
to. Also, I can WHOOSH! get here in a flash, so...

03:10.370 --> 03:13.290
Even so, that's pretty inefficient.

03:14.040 --> 03:17.580
True enough, office matters can
easily be handled by e-mail.

03:18.000 --> 03:25.460
However, I think it is important that a manager maintain
direct communication with the models in his charge.

03:26.130 --> 03:30.180
Well said, Mr. Kitamura!
You take your job so seriously.

03:30.720 --> 03:34.179
I wish MY manager would
learn a thing or two from you.

03:34.180 --> 03:38.099
Ouka, isn't it about time for your job?
It's been a while for you.

03:38.100 --> 03:39.349
Oh, you're right!

03:39.350 --> 03:41.060
Please do your best.

03:42.150 --> 03:46.150
Of course I will! And
so, I bid you farewell!

03:48.070 --> 03:49.400
How are things going, Sonico?

03:49.910 --> 03:51.410
Are you enjoying college?

03:52.120 --> 03:57.580
Yes, it's a lot of fun! And
everyone is really nice to me.

03:58.790 --> 04:00.499
As for your schedule this month...

04:00.500 --> 04:02.629
you've been booked for a studio shoot.

04:02.630 --> 04:02.960
- Photo Shot @ OKSTYLE
- College

04:02.630 --> 04:02.960
- College
- College

04:02.630 --> 04:02.960
- College
- Band @ Ravighe

04:02.630 --> 04:02.960
Zeppelin

04:03.000 --> 04:07.130
You've worked with the client before,
so there shouldn't be any problems.

04:03.180 --> 04:04.340
- Zeppelin
- Band @ Ravighe

04:03.180 --> 04:04.340
- College
- College

04:04.550 --> 04:05.470
- Zeppelin
- Zeppelin

04:04.550 --> 04:05.470
Commercial Audition (1)

04:05.650 --> 04:06.890
- College
- College

04:05.650 --> 04:06.890
- Zeppelin
- College

04:05.650 --> 04:06.890
- College
- Commercial Audition (2)

04:05.650 --> 04:06.890
- Commercial Audition (1)
- Band @ NSS

04:07.630 --> 04:10.680
Sir! I'll do my absolute best.

04:11.470 --> 04:16.560
One more thing: Can you take time off from
school and work from the 5th to the 7th?

04:16.810 --> 04:19.480
Um, for what reason?

04:19.850 --> 04:25.230
A back-cover photo shoot for Yamakawa
Shoten's weekly Young Spawn magazine.

04:25.650 --> 04:27.029
"Young Spawn"?

04:27.030 --> 04:33.080
The Ripe
Young Body
of a
Rebellious Girl

04:27.860 --> 04:31.070
It's a manga anthology sold at
kiosks and convenience stores.

04:31.071 --> 04:32.285
Shoko Matsumoto

04:32.286 --> 04:37.580
It's a mid-level publication, but it's still a
cut above the magazine work you've done so far.

04:33.330 --> 04:37.590
Akiko Kato

04:37.950 --> 04:40.749
Wow, wow, wow! Will I be okay?

04:40.750 --> 04:43.630
W-working for a super magazine like that?!

04:44.000 --> 04:47.090
I can understand how you'd
be nervous, but please don't worry.

04:47.670 --> 04:51.880
Your shoot will be done by Shinji Kishikawa,
a big name in portrait photography.

04:52.430 --> 04:56.180
With Mr. Kishikawa on this,
we're sure to get great results.

04:56.600 --> 04:58.140
O-okay.

04:58.930 --> 05:00.849
Incidentally, the shoot will be...

05:00.850 --> 05:05.860
SONICO
GOES TO OKINAWA

05:01.480 --> 05:03.060
in Okinawa.

05:06.360 --> 05:07.819
Okinawa, huh?

05:07.820 --> 05:09.400
You're lucky, Nico.

05:09.940 --> 05:13.820
It's rainy here, but you'll be
enjoying summer in no time at all.

05:14.360 --> 05:17.119
I can't get myself to look forward to it.

05:17.120 --> 05:22.789
This is a huge job, so the pressure is...
I have to do my best!

05:22.790 --> 05:25.000
Oh, Nico, you'll do just fine.

05:25.290 --> 05:27.540
Thank you very much, Fuuri.

05:27.790 --> 05:31.339
If you can, you should bring back
some pineapples and mangoes.

05:31.340 --> 05:35.219
And Agu pork, soki noodles,
chinsuko cookies, salted sembei,

05:35.220 --> 05:39.139
mint cane sugar, kasa rice cakes,
sweet potato tarts, bitter melon,

05:39.140 --> 05:43.020
H-hold on! Let me write this down.
sea grapes and sata andagi donuts, please!

05:43.310 --> 05:44.689
Uh, okay...

05:44.690 --> 05:48.939
But, Nico, a shoot in Okinawa
means a swimsuit, right?

05:48.940 --> 05:52.610
Y-yeah, it probably does.

05:53.190 --> 05:59.780
Young Spawn is a boy's magazine, so the clothes
will be super racy, right? It's sure to be a bikini.

06:01.620 --> 06:05.080
Suzu. You shouldn't tease her.

06:05.370 --> 06:11.840
Besides, she's represented by a top-notch
manager. She won't have to worry about that.

06:12.460 --> 06:19.390
Yeah! But he's always helping me out,
so I'm a bother to him every day...

06:21.220 --> 06:24.889
I want to go above and
beyond for this shoot!

06:24.890 --> 06:25.890
Yay!

06:26.900 --> 06:28.560
Thanks so much, Mr. Kitamura!

06:28.060 --> 06:28.860
Yamakawa Shoten

06:28.861 --> 06:32.150
I know you've been waiting. Sorry to
have you come all the way out here.

06:32.860 --> 06:40.030
Not at all, Mr. Endo. You have my genuine thanks
for choosing Sonico for this particular endeavor.

06:40.280 --> 06:44.790
C'mon, why so formal?
You and I are friends, right?

06:45.000 --> 06:47.960
What do you say we grab a drink after this?

06:48.330 --> 06:50.420
Indeed. I shall join you.

06:53.380 --> 06:58.010
The concept for the shoot is
"an Okinawan vacation with my boyfriend."

06:58.260 --> 07:04.350
I know Mr. Kishikawa is sure to capture
Sonico's bright, energetic personality.

07:04.810 --> 07:06.480
That's wonderful!

07:06.770 --> 07:10.150
Seeing Sonico on vacation
in a sorta daring outfit...

07:10.650 --> 07:12.150
I can't wait.

07:12.820 --> 07:15.819
I ask that it not be anything too drastic.

07:15.820 --> 07:21.239
C'mon, I know that! Don't give me
such a scary look, Mr. Kitamura.

07:21.240 --> 07:22.410
I am smiling.

07:23.410 --> 07:24.950
I am smiling...

07:26.000 --> 07:30.880
They get fed twice, morning and night. And they
use these sheets to go to the bathroom on...

07:31.460 --> 07:36.970
Yes, I know. I've watched them
for you several times. Right?

07:42.140 --> 07:43.140
Sonico!

07:43.510 --> 07:44.639
We're gonna drive you.

07:44.640 --> 07:45.770
Climb on in!

07:46.270 --> 07:51.350
Mr. Tomi! Mr. Yasu! Thank you very much.
I really appreciate it!

07:53.730 --> 07:55.610
I'll be back!

07:55.940 --> 07:57.150
See you soon.

07:57.320 --> 08:02.870
Suiheisen ni mukatte
I headed for the horizon

08:04.530 --> 08:10.210
Fukinukeru kaze Oikaketa
Chasing after a wind that's blown past

08:11.420 --> 08:14.749
Furimukeba soko ni wa itsudatte
If I turn around, it will always be there

08:14.750 --> 08:16.470
GAL Airlines Flight Ticket

08:18.590 --> 08:22.760
Kimi kara no PRISM
The prism I got from you

08:23.090 --> 08:24.890
Ai shiteru I love you

08:25.390 --> 08:28.640
SHINY LIGHT, mitsumetai
Shiny light, I want to share

08:28.850 --> 08:32.020
Suikomarete yuku, sono hitomi
Those eyes draw me in

08:32.480 --> 08:35.770
Eien o kanjita yo!
I felt eternity!

08:36.020 --> 08:39.570
Whoa, whoa

08:39.650 --> 08:41.970
Wow, wow, wow, wow! I-it's Okinawa!

08:41.971 --> 08:44.805
Komorebi abiru natsu no hi
A summer day bathed in streaming sunlight

08:44.806 --> 08:48.040
It's just like on TV and in
pictures! It's SO Okinawa!

08:48.041 --> 08:53.500
Yureru kozue ni sasowareta
Beckoned by the swaying treetops

08:50.120 --> 08:54.080
If you keep up with your modeling,
you could come here all the time.

08:54.380 --> 08:58.090
Yes! I'll work as hard as I
can to make that happen!

08:54.750 --> 08:58.759
Me o tojite negai o kaketa no
I closed my eyes and made a wish

08:58.760 --> 09:00.010
Mr. Kitamura!

09:00.760 --> 09:02.925
Over here! I've come to pick you up.

09:02.926 --> 09:08.100
"Kimi to no kono hibi o itsumademo"
"Let these days with you last forever"

09:04.890 --> 09:07.060
Sorry for the trouble, Mr. Endo.

09:07.470 --> 09:10.270
Not at all. I'm sure you
have a lot of luggage.

09:08.770 --> 09:11.330
SHINY LIGHT! Kanaetai!
Shiny light! I want my wish to come true!

09:11.331 --> 09:14.730
How do you do, Sonico?
I'm Endo from Yamakawa Shoten.

09:12.190 --> 09:15.045
Hikari no mukou ni mieru mirai
A future I can see beyond the light

09:15.046 --> 09:16.415
N-nice to meet you!

09:16.416 --> 09:19.030
Saikou no TWO SHOT
The greatest pic, just the two of us

09:19.031 --> 09:22.950
Thank you for the opportunity to work
with you. My name is Super Sonico.

09:19.360 --> 09:22.780
Whoa, whoa

09:23.110 --> 09:26.240
SHINY LIGHT! Tsutaetai!
Shiny light! I want to tell you!

09:23.280 --> 09:27.240
I'll do my absolute best to
make sure things go smoothly!

09:27.241 --> 09:29.910
Hikari o mezashite hashittara
If I run, aiming for the light

09:27.910 --> 09:29.910
Well, climb aboard.

09:30.450 --> 09:33.460
Shinjite, uketomete!
Believe it, accept it!

09:33.580 --> 09:37.750
You'll meet the staff once you've
rested at the hotel for a bit.

09:33.750 --> 09:37.170
Whoa, whoa

09:37.670 --> 09:44.470
Kimi no CAMERA mahou mitai ne
Your camera is like magic, huh?

09:38.090 --> 09:41.169
From there, we'll all have dinner together.

09:41.170 --> 09:43.170
Okay. Understood!

09:44.840 --> 09:46.765
Boku o fushigi ni...
Strangely manipulating me

09:46.766 --> 09:51.520
Everyone, thank you for coming out all this
way. I'm Endo, and I'll be overseeing the shoot.

09:51.930 --> 09:57.980
Uh, let's just do some simple introductions.
This is our model, Super Sonico.

09:58.440 --> 10:02.490
My name is Super Sonico.
It's a pleasure to meet you!

10:03.320 --> 10:05.110
And her manager, Mr. Kitamura.

10:05.410 --> 10:08.450
I'm Kitamura. Thank
you for choosing Sonico.

10:09.280 --> 10:11.080
Next up, our photographer.

10:11.330 --> 10:12.750
I'm Kishikawa.

10:13.410 --> 10:14.910
I'm Sato, his assistant.

10:15.620 --> 10:17.130
I'm Suzuki. Ditto.

10:17.830 --> 10:19.340
On makeup, I'm Adachi.

10:20.210 --> 10:22.090
I'm Ikehata, the stylist.

10:22.340 --> 10:23.629
Thank you very much.

10:23.630 --> 10:24.220
Thank you so much!
Thank you very much.

10:24.221 --> 10:25.260
Thank you so much!

10:25.930 --> 10:30.930
Well, I've made a reservation for us
at the restaurant. Let's get going!

10:36.940 --> 10:39.520
It all tastes so good!

10:42.190 --> 10:46.780
I wish I could share this with Suzu
and Fuuri and Grandma, too.

10:47.490 --> 10:48.490
Sonico.

10:49.070 --> 10:53.160
Don't eat too much. Your
shoot kicks off tomorrow.

10:53.450 --> 10:56.330
I-I'm sorry, Mr. Manager.

10:58.120 --> 11:03.130
No worries. Eat up! Your healthy
vigor is what gives you your charm.

11:03.340 --> 11:06.719
Eat up, then give tomorrow
everything you've got!

11:06.720 --> 11:11.600
O-okay! I'll, BAM! give it my all!

11:15.640 --> 11:17.020
Good night.

11:17.350 --> 11:18.730
See you tomorrow.

11:20.560 --> 11:21.650
Mr. Kitamura!

11:22.730 --> 11:25.940
The night's still young. What do you say?

11:26.320 --> 11:28.400
Indeed. I shall join you.

11:28.820 --> 11:33.490
Sonico, we leave at 7:00 a.m. tomorrow.
Try to get to bed early.

11:33.790 --> 11:35.790
Sure. Understood!

11:36.200 --> 11:41.460
Good night, Mr. Manager.
Mr. Endo, good night.

11:41.960 --> 11:43.750
Good night, Sonico.

11:54.060 --> 11:57.296
My Account
Super Sonico
Super Sonico
Well, goodnight everyone~
Super Sonico
First day of the shoot is over.
Good work, everyone!
Gonna do my best tomorrow too~

11:57.320 --> 11:58.320
INTERNATIONAL
STREET

11:59.890 --> 12:01.900
- OKINAWAN SPECIALTIES
- PUB CHURA CHURA

11:59.890 --> 12:01.900
OPEN

12:03.230 --> 12:04.980
That's why, Mr. Endo...

12:05.530 --> 12:10.450
I just! I want to make
Sonico into a first-rate model!

12:10.780 --> 12:13.280
Sure, she's a SMIDGE shy,

12:13.620 --> 12:16.369
but that smile of hers
when she overcomes it...!

12:16.370 --> 12:18.539
Mr. Endo? Are you listening? Mr. Endo!

12:18.540 --> 12:19.869
M'yeah, list'ng...

12:19.870 --> 12:23.749
RIIIIGHT?! I knew y'thought so, too!

12:23.750 --> 12:26.460
Yesss, you TOTALLY get it.

12:28.630 --> 12:29.759
This awamori is delicious.

12:29.760 --> 12:30.840
Um...

12:32.050 --> 12:34.800
Sorry, but are you with
an entertainment agency?

12:35.010 --> 12:39.640
Correct! Indeed I am. I'm
here for a model shoot...

12:40.310 --> 12:43.150
WITH HER! Our mini-celeb Super Sonico!

12:43.480 --> 12:45.439
She's very cute!

12:45.440 --> 12:46.900
Don't gotta tell me!

12:48.480 --> 12:52.320
Um, would you mind if
I asked you something?

12:53.110 --> 12:57.489
Of course. I am especially
keen to talk business.

12:57.490 --> 12:59.199
Is that so?!

12:59.200 --> 13:01.290
Why, of course!

13:04.710 --> 13:06.290
Another drink!

13:13.260 --> 13:17.100
Good morning. I'm
sorry to keep you waiting.

13:17.560 --> 13:19.969
You're actually 20 minutes early.

13:19.970 --> 13:24.650
Huh? Um, am I here too far ahead of time?

13:24.850 --> 13:28.270
No, it's fine. Well, please get in.

13:39.620 --> 13:41.870
Sonico is all set.

13:42.580 --> 13:44.580
Okay, here we go, Sonico.

13:44.790 --> 13:47.710
S-Sir. Thank you very much!

13:47.960 --> 13:51.879
Mr. Endo? Isn't that
suit a little revealing?

13:51.880 --> 13:55.049
That's normal for boys'
magazines these days.

13:55.050 --> 13:56.389
Even so...

13:56.390 --> 13:58.430
That's it, Sonico!

14:05.560 --> 14:09.190
She's looking great. Gotta
hand it to Mr. Kishikawa!

14:09.820 --> 14:12.650
Just don't push the
limits any further, please.

14:12.820 --> 14:14.240
Yes, understood.

14:44.890 --> 14:46.640
Okay, we're done!

14:46.850 --> 14:50.940
That's it for today's shoot. Good job, all!

14:51.190 --> 14:55.650
Thank you very much.
And thank you all, too.

14:55.900 --> 15:01.870
We got some great shots. If we keep
this up, we'll wrap by tomorrow morning.

15:02.700 --> 15:05.959
If we have time, you
can do some sightseeing.

15:05.960 --> 15:11.090
Oh! Thanks so much! I'll
do my best tomorrow, too!

15:11.590 --> 15:14.340
Is there someplace you'd like to go?

15:12.180 --> 15:14.010
OKINAWA'S
AQUARIUMS

15:14.340 --> 15:20.140
Well, an aquarium would be great.
I want to see a bottlenose dolphin!

15:26.850 --> 15:30.230
Hello, Mr. Kitamura!
I've been waiting for you.

15:30.940 --> 15:31.940
Who are you?

15:32.270 --> 15:38.529
Oh, come on. I'm Kakazu, the guy from
the bar last night. The video producer.

15:38.530 --> 15:39.530
What?

15:39.660 --> 15:42.410
Super Sonico, are you ready?

15:42.660 --> 15:46.250
Huh? Um, ready for what?

15:47.080 --> 15:48.620
JUST WHO ARE YOU?

15:48.790 --> 15:52.630
Mr. Kitamura, don't
tell me you've forgotten!

15:52.960 --> 15:59.430
We had drinks last night and talked about Sonico.
You said she could be in my video, didn't you?

16:01.340 --> 16:04.970
I talked to your agency this
morning. Here's the contract.

16:06.350 --> 16:10.899
Um, Mr. Kakazu... I-I'm terribly sorry,
but Sonico has just now finished a shoot.

16:10.900 --> 16:15.149
She's quite tired, so...

16:15.150 --> 16:18.190
Come on! My staff's been waiting!

16:18.530 --> 16:20.280
I don't mind at all.

16:21.570 --> 16:29.500
You're my manager, and you got this job
for my sake. I'll do the best that I can!

16:29.830 --> 16:31.810
Thank goodness! Here,
Sonico. It's the script.

16:30.580 --> 16:33.040
EPISODE 125:
SQUID ALIEN RUNS AMOKI

16:31.811 --> 16:33.040
SEA SQUADRON

16:33.880 --> 16:40.799
Um, the "script"? Is this a
part on a soap opera, maybe?

16:40.800 --> 16:42.509
Oh, you'll be fine.

16:42.510 --> 16:45.850
We're just shooting one scene,
and there's not much dialogue.

16:50.350 --> 16:52.269
Hey, sorry for the wait.

16:52.270 --> 16:54.439
You're late, Kakazu!

16:54.440 --> 17:01.699
Yeah, sorry 'bout that. But the guest I
brought is ROCKIN'! Sonico, if you please.

17:01.700 --> 17:05.569
Um, my name is Super Sonico.

17:05.570 --> 17:10.999
I don't think I'm that good an actress,
so I might just be a huge bother...

17:11.000 --> 17:13.829
But I'll do my absolute best.

17:13.830 --> 17:15.670
Thank you all very much!

17:17.210 --> 17:22.050
Scene 126: A young girl is attacked
by the Red Tide Corps.

17:22.430 --> 17:24.970
The Chura Rangers show up to save her.

17:25.430 --> 17:28.100
The girl can just ad lib "No!" and such.

17:28.350 --> 17:31.100
Ah. S-Sir! Understood!

17:31.930 --> 17:35.479
Monster and Chura Rangers,
do the same shtick as always, please.

17:35.480 --> 17:36.980
Sir!

17:38.020 --> 17:39.939
Scene 126!

17:39.940 --> 17:41.690
And... Action!

17:41.990 --> 17:44.859
Suuuup, sup, sup, sup, sup?!

17:44.860 --> 17:46.030
Eeek!

17:46.320 --> 17:48.159
Suuuup, sup, sup?!

17:48.160 --> 17:50.699
Uh, yeah. Stop.

17:50.700 --> 17:54.669
Suuuup, sup, sup, sup, sup, sup?!

17:54.670 --> 17:57.709
Where are your sea grapes, Sonico?

17:57.710 --> 17:59.880
Please, stop!

18:02.010 --> 18:05.090
What is the point of this shoot?

18:05.300 --> 18:07.640
It's the crux of the whole show.

18:09.100 --> 18:13.430
Each episode, our featured girl gets
ravaged by a costumed monster.

18:13.730 --> 18:18.729
You've really brought me a great heroine!
We'll get more viewers.

18:18.730 --> 18:20.399
I'm sure of it!

18:20.400 --> 18:21.440
You fool!

18:25.860 --> 18:28.409
Where are your sea grapes, Sonico?!

18:28.410 --> 18:31.240
Are they here? Or here?!

18:31.830 --> 18:34.410
Miss Sonico. This is your line!

18:36.040 --> 18:37.750
S-somebody...

18:39.500 --> 18:40.800
Somebody...

18:42.210 --> 18:45.090
Somebody, please help me!

18:47.800 --> 18:49.260
Sonico!

18:50.810 --> 18:51.810
BLRGH!

18:56.100 --> 18:58.400
M-Mr. Manager?

18:59.360 --> 19:03.359
The hell you think you're doin' to Sonico?!

19:03.360 --> 19:04.860
Wh-what gives?

19:05.610 --> 19:08.700
Such tentacular immorality...

19:08.910 --> 19:10.490
Why do you have a sword?!

19:10.700 --> 19:14.700
To defile Sonico... defile Sonico...

19:15.040 --> 19:17.330
I shan't allow it!

19:18.670 --> 19:21.290
I'm being judged! Save me, Chura Rangers!

19:23.250 --> 19:25.090
I'm very sorry.

19:25.340 --> 19:29.590
I accepted the job without
understanding what it entailed.

19:30.090 --> 19:33.310
No, I'm the one who's sorry.

19:33.640 --> 19:36.810
I have to do the best I
can, no matter what the job.

19:38.770 --> 19:42.900
To be honest, I was a little scared.

19:43.440 --> 19:49.030
So, when you came to
save me... Um, I was glad!

19:49.570 --> 19:51.450
Thank you very much.

19:52.660 --> 19:56.039
Sonico. I'll be honest, too.

19:56.040 --> 19:58.709
When you first joined the agency,

19:58.710 --> 20:03.170
you didn't have the right personality for this
business, so I didn't think you'd last long.

20:05.750 --> 20:11.470
U-um... My name is Super Sonico.
Thank you very much.

20:12.300 --> 20:15.100
I am Kitamura, your manager.

20:15.640 --> 20:18.770
Sir! It's a pleasure to meet you.

20:20.600 --> 20:27.030
True, you were awkward.
You seemed utterly naïve. However...

20:27.150 --> 20:29.900
The moment I saw you
smile, I was convinced.

20:30.990 --> 20:36.540
Yours is a smile that could lift
anyone's spirits. That's why I...

20:40.790 --> 20:44.080
Sonico. I may not be the perfect manager,

20:44.380 --> 20:47.000
but I hope to continue working with you.

20:49.970 --> 20:51.630
Good morning!

20:52.550 --> 20:56.350
Uh, we still have 30 minutes to go...

20:57.260 --> 21:02.059
Wow, wow! Did I come too early again?!

21:02.060 --> 21:04.519
You're quite enthusiastic, Sonico.

21:04.520 --> 21:07.110
Well, let's do our best today, too!

21:07.610 --> 21:11.150
Sir! Thank you very much!

21:24.460 --> 21:27.380
Kaze ni yureru
Beneath the palm trees

21:27.670 --> 21:30.590
Yashi no ki no shita
That sway in the breeze

21:30.840 --> 21:36.930
Aoku sunda odayaka na umi
Lies a tranquil sea, blue and clear

21:37.350 --> 21:43.270
WOW, akogareteta
Wow, it's what I've longed for

21:43.520 --> 21:49.690
Shiroku hikaru namiuchigiwa de
To be on a shining white beach

21:49.940 --> 21:55.990
Mizu to asobu, kodomo mitai ni
And play in the water like a kid

21:56.320 --> 22:02.330
WOW, koronde nureta
Wow, I fell and got wet

22:02.660 --> 22:08.750
Natsu no ILLUSION, nanika ga kawaru
Summer's illusion, something will change

22:09.090 --> 22:15.010
Boku wa boku no shinjita michi o yuku yo
I'll go along the road I've believed in

22:15.470 --> 22:18.390
I want to be a rock star

22:18.600 --> 22:24.440
Yume no tame ni chiisa na koto mo For my
dreams, I'll go after even the small things

22:24.810 --> 22:28.149
Zenryoku zenshin, hai! POSE! (Hai!)
Full speed ahead, okay! Pose! (Okay!)

22:28.150 --> 22:31.070
I want to be a rock star

22:31.280 --> 22:37.160
Itsuka mita chiisa na koro no
Like a hero I saw once

22:37.530 --> 22:41.450
HERO mitai ni, itsudemo SMILE FOR YOU When
I was little, I'll smile for you anytime

22:41.950 --> 22:44.119
Stop it! Look out, look out!

22:44.120 --> 22:46.040
You're gonna cut me.
You're really gonna cut me!

22:47.670 --> 22:49.919
I'll drown you in Tokyo Bay!

22:49.920 --> 22:51.960
But this is Okinawa!

22:52.380 --> 22:57.220
And so, with the help of their friend Demon Mask,
the Chura Rangers restored peace to Okinawa.

22:57.760 --> 23:01.100
Thank you, Chura Rangers!
Thank you, Demon Mask!

23:03.430 --> 23:06.020
You got a big part in this!

23:07.190 --> 23:09.230
Why did this happen to me?

23:10.060 --> 23:10.940
Mr. Kitamura?

23:11.070 --> 23:15.690
We've gotten an offer from a Mr. Kakazu
from an Okinawan video production company.

23:15.900 --> 23:17.820
It's for YOU.

23:18.910 --> 23:21.370
NO THANK YOU!

23:24.960 --> 23:32.960
Next Episode Preview

23:25.790 --> 23:28.960
Back then, I loved rock and roll.

23:29.080 --> 23:36.130
I wanted to express myself directly.
And that was when I met her.

23:37.310 --> 23:39.980
Daydream

23:37.550 --> 23:39.720
Next time: "Daydream."
